\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {(a)} Under age-$D$ sensing the achievable $(\rho ,g)$ pairs form the shaded hull. Fixed budgets lie on the diagonal $g=\rho $, and the closed-loop optimum sits a vertical $\Delta (D)=\tfrac  12 r(D)$ above it (Thm.~\ref {thm:limit}). \textbf  {(b)} The same value $\tfrac  12 e^{-D/\tau _c}$ over the sensing-age and coherence-time plane with $\tau _c$ on a log scale. Points are the measured Markov contention sweep of Cor.~\ref {cor:imp}, each shaded by the adaptive controller's closed-loop fraction, opening onto the fixed budget as $D$ crosses $\tau _c$.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:theory}{{2}{4}{\textbf {(a)} Under age-$D$ sensing the achievable $(\rho ,g)$ pairs form the shaded hull. Fixed budgets lie on the diagonal $g=\rho $, and the closed-loop optimum sits a vertical $\Delta (D)=\tfrac 12 r(D)$ above it (Thm.~\ref {thm:limit}). \textbf {(b)} The same value $\tfrac 12 e^{-D/\tau _c}$ over the sensing-age and coherence-time plane with $\tau _c$ on a log scale. Points are the measured Markov contention sweep of Cor.~\ref {cor:imp}, each shaded by the adaptive controller's closed-loop fraction, opening onto the fixed budget as $D$ crosses $\tau _c$}{figure.2}{}}
